  No executable Python code depends on bwc. Remaining matches are in documentation, historical/reference artifacts, existing sample
  data, and generated bwc validation outputs. The file-level remaining match list includes docs like README.md, DEPENDENCY_REPORT.md,
  existing sample/reference files like raw_audio/bwc.wav, ground_truth_json/bwc.json, ground_truth_rttm/bwc.rttm, phase19_reference/...,
  legacy generated outputs/reports, and new validation artifacts named bwc_*.

  Usage

  python run_phase20.py --file bwc
  python run_phase20.py --file traffic_stop
  python run_phase20.py --file traffic_stop --overwrite

  Sequential recordings are independent by construction: all generated pipeline paths derive from --file, so traffic_stop writes
  traffic_stop_* artifacts and does not overwrite bwc_* artifacts. One limitation: --overwrite for an existing JSON requires
  ground_truth/<file>.txt; the current bwc sample has existing JSON/RTTM, so the non-overwrite command works and skips conversion.
